<newsitem itemid="50643" id="root" date="1996-09-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>FRANCE: BNP 1996 first-half result details.</title>
<headline>BNP 1996 first-half result details.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detailed BNP results for first half of 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of francs unless otherwise indicated)</p>
<p>    Net attrib			     1,735     vs    966</p>
<p>    Net					1,844     vs  1,056</p>
<p>    Pre-tax pre-exceptional	    2,660     vs  1,548</p>
<p>    Net banking income		  19,223     vs 18,334</p>
<p>    Operating				5,119     vs  4,336</p>
<p>    Operating costs		     14,104     vs 13,968</p>
<p>    Net new provisions		   2,459     vs  2,818</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    France risks			   2,016     vs  2,469</p>
<p>    International risks		    443     vs    349</p>
<p>    Exceptional, various items	   192     vs     70</p>
<p>    Tax charge				 868     vs    733</p>
<p>    Equity accounting			276     vs    355</p>
<p>    Goodwill amortisation	  loss   32     vsloss 44</p>
<p>    Shareholder funds (billion)	 50.3     vs   48.6</p>
<p>    Solveny ratio (percent)		9.1     vs    9.1</p>
<p>    of which tier one			5.5     vs    5.5</p>
<p>Note: BNP said in a statement total outstanding loan levels were down 2.2 percent on average in the first half and that the desposit side saw a rise of 9.1 percent.</p>
<p>Managed capital increased 15.1 percent to 275 billion francs while assets managed for clients rose 22.6 percent to 86 billion from 70 billion.</p>
<p>Capital managed breaks down as follows (in billions):</p>
<p>    Life insurance			    91	vs     67</p>
<p>    Money market funds			96	vs     86</p>
<p>    Other unit trusts			 88	vs     86</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
